1	// Package embed implements Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B: text in, a 1024-dimensional
2	// unit vector out.
3	//
4	// The transformer is not written here. It is the same `Qwen3Model` as
5	// Z-Image's text encoder, which `zimage/qwen` already implements on the CPU
6	// and on the device, 36 layers of 2560 against 28 of 1024 -- so this package
7	// is the four things an *embedding* model has that a text encoder does not,
8	// and nothing else:
9	//
10	//   - every layer runs, where the encoder stops one short (`hidden_states[-2]`);
11	//   - the final `norm` runs after them;
12	//   - the vector is the **last token's** row (`1_Pooling` asks for
13	//     pooling_mode_lasttoken), and the last token is the `<|endoftext|>` the
14	//     tokenizer's post-processor appends -- see tokenizer.go, it is the
15	//     likeliest silent bug in the whole vertical;
16	//   - the row is L2-normalised, so a dot product is a cosine.
17	//
18	// Instructions (`Instruct: …\nQuery:…`) are part of the input *text* rather
19	// than of the model, so they are a function here and a request field at the
20	// API layer, not something Embed does behind the caller's back.
21	package embed
22	
23	import (
24		"fmt"
25		"math"
